---
// "Why Board-Certified Matters" blurb + the Staff grid. Ported verbatim from
// tools/snapshots/meet-the-team.html (search "meet-the-team-stafff" — note
// the live triple-f typo in that class, kept as-is).
//
// Despite a `staff` collection existing in the CMS, this section on the live
// page is static markup — there is no w-dyn-list here, just one hardcoded
// .div-block-3 card for Kathy G. Reproduced static per the brief rather than
// wired to getCollection('staff').
//
// Kathy's <h1 class="staff-name"> is the SECOND <h1> on this page (the page
// header's "The veterinary internal medicine group" is the first) — a real
// duplicate-h1 accessibility/SEO issue on the live site, replicated
// deliberately rather than silently demoted to an h2. See the about-page
// report.
import staffImage from '~/assets/FD4A0017.jpg';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<div class="general-section no-margin new-padding dark-color-bg">
  <div class="container meet-the-team-stafff">
    <div class="text-center margin-15">
      <h4 class="section-title-top white center">Board certification isn&rsquo;t a title, it&rsquo;s a standard.</h4>
      <h2 class="section-title white">Why Board-Certified Matters</h2>
      <div class="section-line-animation-div">
        <div class="color-line white"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="center-content">
      <p class="about-the-team-paragraph">
        A board-certified internal medicine specialist (DACVIM-SAIM) has completed extensive advanced training
        beyond veterinary school, including a competitive residency and rigorous examinations. While many providers
        offer &ldquo;specialty&rdquo; services after short courses, board certification represents a higher standard
        of expertise and that difference matters when your pet&rsquo;s health is on the line. At VIMG, diagnostics
        and recommendations are performed and interpreted by the specialist who sees your pet, in real time,
        leading to clearer answers, fewer unnecessary procedures, and care that always puts your pet first.
      </p>
      <h2 class="section-title white">Staff</h2>
      <div class="w-layout-grid staff-members-grid">
        <div class="div-block-3">
          <Image src={staffImage} alt="" class="image-5" loading="lazy" />
          <h1 class="staff-name">Kathy G.</h1>
          <div class="section-line-animation-team-div">
            <div class="color-line-services"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="staff-position">Manager</div>
          <p class="staff-bio">
            Kathy has been a dedicated Veterinary Technician since 2010. She earned her Associate of Science degree
            in Veterinary Technology and has gained valuable experience in emergency, general practice, and
            specialty veterinary settings. She brings years of hands-on experience and a genuine love for animals
            and to everything she does.<br /><br />
            She is now thrilled to step into a leadership role and looks forward to serving as Practice Manager at
            VIMG, where she can help guide the team while continuing to provide excellent care for pets and their
            families. In her free time, she enjoys playing the piano, singing, and making outdoor memories with her
            husband and kids.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
